// Edge <-> Avatar contract. One bidi stream per voice session: the Go media
// edge sends the session's two audio timelines (what the agent is about to say
// and what the user is saying) as paired 16 kHz frames; the avatar service
// renders a talking-head video from them and streams encoded H.264 back, which
// the edge packetizes onto a WebRTC video track.
//
// The avatar service is deliberately a peer of the edge, not of the
// orchestrator: the edge already holds both audio streams, owns the playout
// clock they must be synchronised against, and owns the peer connection the
// video has to leave on.
